        "response": {
          "content": "### [P2] Restore the zero accumulator\n**Source-confirmed regression; advisory.** Your stated contract requires empty arrays to return zero. In `sum.ts:1`, removing the initial `0` makes `sum([])` throw `TypeError`: `reduce` has neither an initial accumulator nor an element to use. The fixed base returned `0`.\n\nThe unchanged `emptyTotal()` in `caller.ts:2` explicitly calls `sum([])`, so it now throws. Nonempty dense arrays avoid this exception, but the `number[]` signature permits empty arrays and no guard exists.\n\n**Correction:** restore `values.reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0)`. Add regression tests asserting both `sum([])` and `emptyTotal()` return `0`, plus singleton and multi-element cases.\n\nAll exposed source/base files were read. Test review remains incomplete: no test files were exposed, and no tests were executed.",
